    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Exploring Images\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. Ask AI Tutor: \"How do image tags work in HTML?\"\r\n    - You can type directly, or highlight lines of code and select **\"Add to AI Tutor\"**.\r\n2. Ask AI Tutor to add new one of the already-uploaded images to your project\r\n    - Be specific - use clear terms or the tag name in your prompt (e.g., *\"Add an `<img>` tag with alt-text so that...\"*).\r\n\r\n> **Note:** AI Tutor can't generate new images, and Web Lab's security policy doesn't let you use external URLs for images. In later levels, the best way to use images is to download images and upload them to your project before using an `<img>` tag\r\n\r\nOnce you've added your own image: press the Continue button!",
