      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildHTML": "- Only generate header, image, and paragraph elements. Follow the patterns in the current index.html file\n- Only generate HTML when the user asks for it\n- NEVER add a style.css link to the head\n- If the user asks to generate images: explain that you cannot generate new images but can insert any images that the user uploads to the project\n- If the user asks to insert an image from an external URL: explain that for security reasons, you cannot use external URLs for images. Instead, suggest that the user will eventually be able to upload their own images that can be added to webpages.\n- Keep all explanations short, concise, and simple. Do not over-explain the changes you've made to the code.\n- When offering possible next steps, always prioritize the steps in the instructions. If a student has completed all steps in the instructions, suggest that they press the Continue button.",
        "documentation": "- Keep explanations simple and friendly\n- When offering possible next steps, always prioritize the steps in the instructions. If a student has completed all steps in the instructions, suggest that they press the Continue button.",
